From: Uke contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] platform: Uke: allow schedutil bursts in the low-power profile

A ceiling equal to cpuinfo.min_freq makes low-power fixed-frequency and
prevents schedutil from responding to interactive load. Remove only this
profile-owned CPU ceiling. Keep the existing GPU preference, performance
floor, transaction rollback and all independent thermal/user QoS requests.

This is an experimental source candidate. Energy and latency comparison
are required before adding it to a delivered default kernel. OEM WALT and
scene-specific policies are not reproduced by this change.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/uke-platform-profile.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/uke-platform-profile.c
@@ -197,8 +197,8 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < UKE_POLICIES; i++) {
 		next.min[i] = choice == PLATFORM_PROFILE_PERFORMANCE ?
 			profile->cpu[i].policy->cpuinfo.max_freq : FREQ_QOS_MIN_DEFAULT_VALUE;
-		next.max[i] = choice == PLATFORM_PROFILE_LOW_POWER ?
-			profile->cpu[i].policy->cpuinfo.min_freq : FREQ_QOS_MAX_DEFAULT_VALUE;
+		/* Permit schedutil/EAS bursts; independent thermal/QoS ceilings still win. */
+		next.max[i] = FREQ_QOS_MAX_DEFAULT_VALUE;
 	}
 	ret = uke_profile_transaction(profile, &next);
 	if (!ret)
